course: dictionary
lesson: 10696
title: Unsaturated: still room to take more
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning, and the words around them show which one you need. Unsaturated is one of those words. «The other parts are protein foods such as beans, eggs, fish and meat, dairy or alternatives, and small amounts of unsaturated oils» is talking about food groups, so unsaturated here means the healthier kind of fat, the sort found in plants and fish.
explain: In science, unsaturated means a liquid can still take in more of something. Imagine adding salt to water one spoon at a time. While the salt keeps dissolving, the solution is unsaturated. When no more salt will dissolve, it is saturated, which means full.
explain: In art, unsaturated colours are pale or greyish, not strong. Always ask: what would fit here? Then try your meaning in the sentence and check that it still makes sense.
fact: Unsaturated means not full, or still able to take more.
fact: Unsaturated fats are found mostly in plants and fish, like olive oil.
fact: Unsaturated fats are usually liquid at room temperature, and they are healthier than saturated fats.
fact: An unsaturated salt water solution can still dissolve more salt. A saturated one cannot.
fact: Unsaturated colours are pale or greyish, not strong or bright.
exercise: In a science lesson, what does an unsaturated salt water solution mean? | It is full, and no more salt can dissolve | *It can still dissolve more salt | It has no water in it at all | It has turned into ice
exercise: Which food is most likely to contain unsaturated fat? | Hard cheese | Butter | Solid lard | *Olive oil
exercise: An artist says her colours are unsaturated. What does this suggest? | Shiny like metal | Full of water | *Pale or greyish, not strong | Bright and loud
test: Unsaturated fats are usually what at room temperature? | Solid like butter | Frozen like ice | *Liquid like oil | Burnt and black
test: A solution is saturated when what happens? | It stops being a liquid | It is so full that no more salt will dissolve | It turns into a gas | *It still has room for more salt to dissolve
exam: «Unsaturated oils» in a food label is talking about fats, so unsaturated means what? | *Healthier fats found mostly in plants and fish | Fizzy like a drink | Full of sugar | Very hot to touch
